### Bug Description
String list entry created by `startStrList` inside a subcategory can open the edit popup normally.
Existing items are displayed in the popup, but **all items cannot be selected or edited**.
- Clicking existing items has no response;
- Cannot delete any item;
- Can click the add button to create a blank new item, but this new blank item also cannot be selected or edited.

The exact same string list entry works perfectly when placed directly in the root category (outside any subcategory).
Other entry types (boolean toggle, text field) inside the same subcategory work without any issues.

### Minimal Reproduce Code
```java
var subCat = entry.startSubCategory(Component.literal("Sub Category"));
// Toggle works fine
subCat.add(entry.startBooleanToggle(Component.literal("Test Toggle"), true)
        .setSaveConsumer(v -> {})
        .build());
// StringList inside subcategory triggers the bug
subCat.add(entry.startStrList(Component.literal("String List"), new ArrayList<>())
        .setSaveConsumer(list -> {})
        .build());
mainCategory.addEntry(subCat.build());

## Observed Behaviour

-  Clicking on the same inputfield twice removes the cursor. Causing the field to be ineditable.
    - At nesting level 0, on Enums, the suggestions remain visible and clickable.
    - At nesting level 1+, on Enums, the suggestions disappear on the second click.
    - Clicking the same inputfield a third time does nothing.
- Fields at nesting level 2+ cannot be edited, unless a field at nesting level 0/1 is clicked first.

## Expected Behaviour

- The behaviour from 1.21.11 is restored.
- Clicking the same inputfield a second time *moves* the cursor to the clicked position.

## Steps to Reproduce

